* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #102, Part of #16)
* WHOLE-CELL comparator-window measurement for the post-layout lock_detector
* arms -- the twin of ../../sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window's
* tb_window.sp.tmpl that the FLAT extraction can run at all. The schematic
* campaign measures the window on a BARE delaywin_hv (the chain element
* alone, `Xw wstep wout vdd 0 delaywin_hv`); the extraction is one flat
* subckt with no isolated chain, but its ERR/ERRD pins are exactly the
* chain's input and output nets, so driving ERR with the same ideal step
* and thresholding ERRD measures the same LOW-to-HIGH propagation -- with
* the rest of the block (the XOR hung on the driver node, the coincidence
* gate and the integrating node) loading the rails exactly as they do in
* the real block. This deck therefore ALSO runs on the as-layout schematic
* variant (derive_ld_as_layout.py's `lock_detector_ep`, same exposed ERR/
* ERRD ports), so the schematic-vs-post-layout window deviation below is a
* controlled A/B: same device set, same stimulus, same contention.
*
* tb_window.sp.tmpl's own stimulus and measurement are kept verbatim: the
* ideal 100 ps-edge step, 20 ns high inside a 60 ns window, `twin_r`/
* `twin_f` measured at VSUP/2 on the rising/falling pair, the same
* .options. UP/DN are tied at 0 V (quiescent XOR, so no input activity
* contaminates the rails during the measurement window); LOCK is left
* undriven (schmitt output-only port) on both arms.
*
* ../run_lock_detector.sh substitutes @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @TEMP@,
* @VSUP@, @VMID@, @TSTEP@, @DUT@ (the netlist to .include -- either the
* as-layout err-ports variant or the pex-to-ngspice.py-rewritten
* extraction), @INST@ (the instantiation: `Xld ... lock_detector_ep` for the
* schematic copy, or the make-inst.py line for the extracted copy), and
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (ngspice's .lib/.include parser does not expand
* environment variables, issue #54).
*
* The extracted netlist declares its own `.GLOBAL vsubs` and ties it to
* ground only through klt's 1e12-ohm DC tie; every extracted net-to-ground
* parasitic capacitor returns to that node, so -- exactly like
* tb_cp_dc_pex.sp.tmpl -- it is held hard at 0 V. The schematic variant
* has no vsubs net; a 0 V source on an otherwise unused node is inert there,
* which keeps the two arms' decks textually identical.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@
.include @INST@

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vsubs vsubs 0 dc 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

* Quiescent inputs on both arms: XOR steady, no input activity.
Vup ld_up 0 dc 0
Vdn ld_dn 0 dc 0

* Ideal step in, 100 ps edges: 20 ns high, then low, inside a 60 ns window,
* so both the rising and the falling propagation delay are measured in one
* transient with the chain fully settled before each edge -- tb_window's
* own waveform, applied to the chain's input pin.
Vstep ld_err 0 pulse(0 @VSUP@ 10n 100p 100p 20n 1000n)

* --- the DUT instantiation (arm-specific, filled from @INST@) is in the
*     include file above: the driver node is wired to ld_err, the chain's
*     output to ld_errd, and UP/DN/VDD/VSS/LOCK per that arm's pin list.

.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13 itl4=5000 gmin=1e-11
.tran @TSTEP@ 60n

.control
run
meas tran twin_r trig v(ld_err) val=@VMID@ rise=1 targ v(ld_errd) val=@VMID@ rise=1
meas tran twin_f trig v(ld_err) val=@VMID@ fall=1 targ v(ld_errd) val=@VMID@ fall=1
print twin_r twin_f
.endc
.end
